msgid "\"{}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md:42
msgid ""
"The functionality of copying bytes from one place to the next remains the "
"same."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md:44
msgid ""
"“However, we need to manually create a slice. To do that, we first need to "
"find the end of the data."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md:47
msgid ""
"“As we’re working with text, we’ll use the C convention of a null-terminated "
"string."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md:50
msgid "Compile the code. See that the output remains the same."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md:52
msgid ""
"“An unsound function can still work correctly for some inputs. Just because "
"your tests pass, does not mean that you have a sound function.”"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md:55
msgid "“Can anyone spot any issues?”"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md:57
msgid "Readability: difficult to quickly scan code"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md:58
msgid "`source` pointer might be null"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md:59
msgid ""
"`source` pointer might be dangling, i.e. point to freed or uninitialized "
"memory"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md:61
msgid "`source` might not be null-terminated"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md:63
msgid ""
"“Assume that we cannot change the function signature, what improvements "
"could we make to the code to address these issues?”"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md:66
msgid ""
"Null pointer: Add null check with early return (`if source.is_null() "
"{ return; }`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md:68
msgid ""
"Readability: Use a well-tested library rather than implementing “find first "
"null byte” ourselves"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md:71
msgid ""
"“Some safety requirements are impossible to defensively check for, however, "
"i.e.:”"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md:74
msgid "dangling pointer"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md:75
msgid "no null termination byte"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md:77
msgid "“How can we make this function sound?”"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md:79
msgid "Either"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md:80
msgid ""
"Change the type of the `source` input argument to something that has a known "
"length, i.e. use a slice like the previous example."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-deep-dive/rules-of-the-game/copying-memory/exposed-unsafe.md:82
msgid "Or"
msgstr ""

